lems. rxn_001 should produce H2O, rxn_002 is an unbalanced and highly compressed syngas homologation, rxn_006 omits water and NH3, and rxn_008 omits H2O and lacks a clear catalytic basis. The internally balanced steps rxn_003, rxn_005, and rxn_007 help, but they do not rescue the pathway as written.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_001\",\n        \"rxn_002\",\n        \"rxn_006\",\n        \"rxn_008\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Correct rxn_001 and rxn_002 stoichiometry and define how HCN and aldehyde are transferred between environments.\",\n        \"Fix rxn_006 to include 2 H2O and NH3.\",\n        \"Add catalyst or mineral detail for rxn_003, rxn_007, and especially rxn_008.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"best_pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n  \"overall_confidence\": 0.34,\n  \"network_feedback\": \"The network is connected and has adequate node count, and several route motifs are chemically recognizable. The chemically strongest steps are rxn_003, rxn_005, and rxn_007. However, the deterministic balance check shows 9 of 12 reactions are unbalanced, so the network is not chemically valid as written. A H2O node is missing even though many steps need it. The required fixes are specific: rxn_001 should be formamide -> HCN + H2O; rxn_002 and rxn_004 need multicarbon CO/H2 stoichiometries and coproducts such as H2O; rxn_006 should consume 2 H2O and release NH3; rxn_008 and rxn_009 should produce H2O; rxn_010 should consume 2 H2O and release NH3; rxn_011 is mis-specified for hydantoin formation and likely needs NH3 removed from the reactant side or replacement by an explicit carbamylation or Bucherer-Bergs sequence; and rxn_012 should consume 2 H2O and release NH3 + CO2. Environmental consistency is only moderate because transport between surface, hydrothermal, and aqueous nonenzymatic settings is implicit, the label biochemical is too vague for a prebiotic environment, and catalysts or minerals are not identif